ion   5 8cm S I x 3 8cm M L x 2 2cm A P  oriented by the surgeon  short suture   superior  long lateral   The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the  evaluation of margins  posterior black  anterior blue  superior red   inferior green  lateral yellow  medial orange  The specimen is received with a  central full thickness defect  2 1 x 2 0cm    which extends through the  anterior and posterior margins  Definitive skin is not identified on the  anterior aspect of the specimen  The specimen is serially sectioned from  superior to inferior into 12 slices  slice 1 equals most superior   In slices  3 7  there is a well delineated  red brown to tan white fibrous  partially  fragmented area  2 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm   grossly consistent with a biopsy cavity   which is 0 1cm from the posterior margin  0 2cm from the anterior margin  REMOVED_DATE  cm from the medial margin  0 4cm from the lateral margin  0 4cm from the  superior margin  and 1 2cm from the inferior margin  Adjacent to the presumed  cavity is abundant chalky gritty yellow tan fat necrosis  The remainder of the  specimen is composed of approximately dense  focally cystic  0 1 0 4cm    fibrous stroma extending to all surgical margins and encompassing the  aforementioned biopsy cavity  and approximately 20  yellow tan lobulated  adipose tissue  No additional discrete lesions are noted   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   slice 3  bisected to include biopsy cavity with closest superior  margin  1 frag each  ESS  Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   slice 4  bisected to include biopsy cavity with closest posterior   lateral  anterior and medial margin  1 frag each  ESS  Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   slice 5  bisected biopsy cavity with adjacent fat necrosis and  additional margins  1 frag each  RSS  Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   slice 6  sectioned biopsy cavity with adjacent fat necrosis and  dense stroma  3 frags total  ESS  Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   slice 7  bisected remaining biopsy cavity with adjacent dense