Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Private Outside MGH MEEI MRN  REMOVED_DATE Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  KAREN A O BRIEN  M D  Resident  Matthew M Johnson  M D  Signed Out by  John H Eichhorn  M D  CLINICAL DATA  64 year old woman with right breast mass    Benign fibroadenoma   other  Patient on hormone replacement therapy  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE BIOPSY  COMPLEX PROLIFERATIVE AND SCLEROSING LESION  FAVOR BENIGN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The biopsy cores show florid ductal epithelial hyperplasia of the usual type accompanied by intervening fibroplasia  By immunohistochemical methods  most of the proliferating epithelial cells express cytokeratin REMOVED_DATE in a pattern consistent with a hyperplastic process  Immunohistochemical staining for epithelial and myoepithelial cell antigens  pan keratin  myosin heavy chain  calponin and p63  fails to show definitive evidence of stromal invasion  Together with the morphological features  the findings favor a benign process such as a florid radial sclerosing lesion  Excision is needed  however  if clinically indicated  to fully sample the mass and to exclude a more serious process  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN only  are seven cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm which are submitted in toto as cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fellow Review by Matthew M Johnson M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST 