Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Pavan K Auluck  M D   Ph D  Reports To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Tissue Processed Reason for Addendum  3  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Status post left breast biopsy  DCIS  ER PR positive  with strong family history  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  SCATTERED FOCI  ADJACENT TO AND AWAY FROM THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE  TINY CLUSTER OF ATYPICAL CELLS IN A LYMPHATIC VESSEL ADJACENT TO THE BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NOTE  There is a cluster of 3 atypical cells within a lymphatic space which is suspicious for but not diagnostic of carcinoma  The differential for these cells includes histiocytes  as there are other lymphatic vessels containing histiocytes in the same region  However  the atypical cells have a higher nuclear to cytoplasmic ratio and sharper cell borders  making them suspicious for epithelial cells  They are not present on the deeper section  and therefore  additional studies cannot be performed  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA  SENTINEL   EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA CELLS IN 2 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  ISOLATED TUMOR CELLS   SEE NOTE   NOTE  There are scattered single cells and small clusters of cells  up to 6 cells  present in the lymph node sinuses which are evident on both HE and keratin immunostained sections  totalling about 45 cells  The cytologic features are consistent carcinoma  Dr  David Wilbur concurs with this interpretation  Studies for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and Her2 neu will be attempted and the results will be reported in an addendum  SKIN  LEFT BREAST ADDITIONAL   EXCISION  SKIN AND SUBCUTANEOUS FAT WITH FAT NECROSIS  HEMORRHAGE  AND FIBROSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  MILDLY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  COLUMNAR CELL TYPE  SCATTERED FOCI  MILD FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  PSEUDOANGIOMATOUS STROMAL HYPERPLASIA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 3 OF 3 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA  SENTINEL   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 2 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE   NOTE  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  SKIN  RIGHT BREAST ADDITIONAL   EXCISION  NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is an 850 gram  26 x 18 x 3 5cm simple mastectomy specimen with axillary tail measuring 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  There is a 4 x 3cm skin ellipse centered around the nipple on the anterior surface  The anterior surface is dark yellow  fatty with no areas of puckering  The posterior surface is yellow red  smooth and glistening  The anterior resection margin is inked blue  the posterior resection margin is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal predominantly dense fibrous breast tissue surrounded peripherally by yellow unremarkable fat  No discrete lesions or otherwise suspicious areas are identified  The axillary tail is dissected to reveal three potential lymph nodes  Representative sections of the breast parenchyma including the deep margin are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The three potential lymph nodes are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME